        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45041769?u=84b77cf7e5ba6819948e59a9a3c208ef60d5b722&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n\n\n\n<hr>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Add the <code class=\"notranslate\">.webmanifest</code> extension with corresponding <code class=\"notranslate\">application/manifest+json</code> MIME type to the list of common MIME types (and extensions).</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Given the recommendations on <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Progressive_web_apps/Manifest#deploying_a_manifest\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Progressive_web_apps/Manifest#deploying_a_manifest</a>, based on the specification in <a href=\"https://w3c.github.io/manifest/#media-type-registration\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://w3c.github.io/manifest/#media-type-registration</a>, this extension and corresponding MIME type is a relevant entry for web-related extensions and MIME types. This should help people more easily recognize webmanifest files and their purpose.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n",
